    {
      "id": 1900,
      "q": 47,
      "section": "Core Subject",
      "text": "What is the value of the eigenvalue of the matrix [2, 1; 1, 2]?",
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "1",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "text": "3",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "-1",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "-3",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "solution": "The characteristic equation of the matrix [2, 1; 1, 2] is |A - λI| = 0, where λ is the eigenvalue. Expanding the determinant, we get (2 - λ)(2 - λ) - 1 = 0, which simplifies to λ^2 - 4λ + 3 = 0. Solving the quadratic equation, we get λ = 1 and λ = 3. Therefore, the eigenvalue of the matrix is 3."
    },
